# What a release archive holds: the source in the tree (the binaries under integrator/bin and graphs/bin, once
# built) and its name in the archive.  A leading '?' marks a file that may be absent (the GPU binaries, when the
# package is built on a machine without CUDA); a trailing '/' a directory, copied whole.  tools/release reads it.
LICENSE	LICENSE
releases/ARCHIVE-README.md	README.md
integrator/bin/rebar_cpu	rebar_cpu
integrator/bin/rebar_cpu-e18	rebar_cpu-e18
integrator/bin/rebar_cpu-e20	rebar_cpu-e20
?integrator/bin/rebar_gpu	rebar_gpu
?integrator/bin/rebar_gpu-e18	rebar_gpu-e18
?integrator/bin/rebar_gpu-e20	rebar_gpu-e20
graphs/bin/topologies	topologies
integrator/data/lists/	lists/
